## Why This Is Asked
This checks understanding of idempotency, at-least-once semantics, and practical CI test design for a queue-driven worker.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent writes and deduplication
- At-least-once vs exactly-once delivery
- Mocking queues, in-memory stores and DB transactions
- CI stability and flaky-test mitigation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo test outline using Jest-like syntax
function testDedupAndWrite(db, queue) {
  const events = [{id: 'e1'}, {id: 'e1'}]; // duplicate
  queue.publish(events[0]);
  queue.publish(events[1]);
  processOnce();
  if (db.count('summary', 'e1') !== 1) throw new Error('duplicate write');
}
```

